  "Question": "The diameters of two circles are \\(8\\) inches and \\(12\\) inches respectively. The ratio of the area of the smaller to the area of the larger circle is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac49\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac94\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A radius is half its diameter, so the smaller and larger circles have radii 4 inches and 6 inches. Using the circle area formula \\(A=\\pi r^2\\), their smaller-to-larger area ratio is\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi\\cdot4^2}{\\pi\\cdot6^2}\n=\\frac{16}{36}=\\frac49.\n\\]\nThe common factor \\(\\pi\\) cancels because we are comparing the two areas. The answer is \\(4/9\\), choice B.",
